        "An explicit counterexample to three-summand Kato-kernel splitting \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem30003045, Laghribi with Aravire/O\u2019Ryan, OWR5/2016 printed251 Question2. Complete negative answer to the proposed universal three-summand Kato-kernel equality: explicit n=1 counterexample over F2(b,z,s,t), degree-four exponent-two purely inseparable L/F, genuine separable quadratic K/F and binary anisotropic bilinear Pfister form. Universal all-rational-parameter norm obstruction proves exclusion from the FULL three-summand sum. The n=0 assertion holds for positive-fold forms. The exact killed mixed generator is an explicit specialization of Aravire-Laghribi-O\u2019Ryan2019 Theorem1.4; target-specific third-summand exclusion is supplied here. Auxiliary exponent-one differentiation shortcut repaired via the valid L+K kernel-sum deduction. No novelty/firstness/current-global-openness certification; inaccessible adjacent bodies and original contextual-exposure limits disclosed. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review or formal proof certification. Two successive fresh no-history complete-package reviews passed the identical release. Four complete algebra runs normal/optimized and18 actual computed wrong-result failures; finite diagnostics supplement universal proof. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1150 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23444050"
